    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "## Problem\n\n#4465 reverted the backend half of the private-hashed-tmux-socket migration (#4393) \u2014 `runtimeselect.New()` now calls `tmux.New(tmux.Options{})` with no `SocketPath`, so `socketForSession`'s `r.socketName` is empty by default and legacy sessions are found directly on the machine's default socket.\n\nHowever, the desktop Electron main process still independently opts every packaged launch back into the private socket:\n\n```\nfrontend/src/main.ts:845\n...(bundledTmuxBinary ? { AO_TMUX_BINARY: bundledTmuxBinary, AO_TMUX_SOCKET_NAME: \"ao\" } : {}),\n```\n\n`tmux.New` reads `AO_TMUX_SOCKET_NAME` from the environment when `Options.SocketName` is empty (`tmux.go:287-289`), so any packaged desktop build with a staged bundled tmux binary \u2014 the common case \u2014 still runs with `socketName = \"ao\"`, and hits the exact symptom #4465 set out to fix.\n\n## Reproduce\n\nOn a machine with tmux sessions that predate this whole migration (i.e. living only on the default socket):\n\n```\n$ /path/to/bundled/tmux -L ao has-session -t <session-id>\nerror connecting to /private/tmp/tmux-<uid>/ao (No such file or directory)\n\n$ /path/to/bundled/tmux -L default has-session -t <session-id>\n(exit 0 \u2014 session is alive)\n```\n\n`socketForSession` (`tmux.go`) only crosses the migration boundary to the legacy default socket when the private-socket probe output matches `sessionMissingOutput` (\"can't find session\"/\"session not found\") or `serverNotRunningOutput` (\"no server running\"). Neither matches \"error connecting ... No such file or directory\" \u2014 the exact message tmux gives when the private socket file was never created, which is guaranteed on first launch of a build with this env var reintroduced against pre-existing legacy sessions. The probe returns `ErrRuntimeProbeInconclusive`, and every legacy session's terminal pane shows \"Terminal disconnected \u2014 reattaching\u2026\" indefinitely, with `reconcile: reap pass failed` / `reaper: probe error reported as failed fact` log spam for every session.\n\n## Why this survived #4465's testing\n\n#4465's revert is real and correct for the backend default, but its own repro/verification path (`env -u AO_TMUX_BINARY ... npm run lint` etc., per the PR body) unsets `AO_TMUX_BINARY`, which also disables the `bundledTmuxBinary` branch in `main.ts` that sets `AO_TMUX_SOCKET_NAME`. So the revert's own verification never exercises the actual packaged-desktop code path where the symptom reappears.\n\n## Fix options\n\n- Drop the `AO_TMUX_SOCKET_NAME: \"ao\"` half of `main.ts:845` (keep `AO_TMUX_BINARY` only) so the packaged desktop app matches the reverted backend default, or\n- If the private socket is still wanted opportunistically from the desktop launcher, extend `socketForSession`'s migration-boundary check to also treat \"error connecting ... no such file or directory\" as definitive (this is what a private socket that was simply never created looks like \u2014 distinct from a running server going transiently unreachable, which the existing `transientServerFailureOutput`/#3475 guard is right to keep ambiguous).\n\n## Verification after fix\n\nOn a machine with pre-existing default-socket sessions, launch the packaged desktop app and confirm the terminal pane attaches immediately instead of showing \"Terminal disconnected \u2014 reattaching\u2026\", and `daemon.log` has no `reconcile reap ...: probe: ... liveness probe inconclusive: error connecting` entries for those sessions.\n\n## Related\n- #4465 (this issue's cause \u2014 the backend-only revert)\n- #4393 (original migration)\n",
